claim.claim-text:
a stock container zone (20) configured to store a plurality of stock containers (202);
a transfer robot (40) configured to transport the stock containers (202); and
a picking zone (10) configured for a picking operator to pick target goods from the stock container (202) transported by the transfer robot (40); wherein:

the picking zone (10) comprises at least one picking station (1), each picking station (1) comprising two picking passages (121) and two picking points (122) respectively located on the two picking passages (121);
each picking point (122) is configured for the picking operator to pick the target goods;
each picking passage (121) is U-shaped and configured to provide a traveling route for the transfer robot (40) to enter the picking station (1) and pass through the picking point (122) on each picking passage (121) in each picking station (1) and leave the picking station (1).

during walking on a route of the transfer robot (40), detect whether a cell near a route point ahead is occupied, and in response to the cell near the route point ahead being possible to be applied for at the same time, use the route point as a rotation point;
when the transfer robot (40) arrives at the rotation point, occupy a surrounding cell, and in response to the occupation is unsuccessful, control the transfer robot (40) to continue to walk;
before the transfer robot (40) arrives at a picking point (122), if the stock container (202) is not rotated on the route, control the transfer robot (40) to enter a rotation zone set for the picking point (122); and
in a case where the stock container (202) that has been rotated still needs to be rotated, determine in situ whether a surrounding cell is possible to be occupied, and in response to the surrounding cell being possible to be occupied, control the transfer robot (40) to occupy the surrounding cell, and in response to the surrounding cell being not possible to be occupied, control the transfer robot (40) to enter the picking station (1) again and continue to queue and enter a rotation point;
and preferably, a straightline and arc line tangent route or a polyline route is used in the rotation zone to perform stock container rotation.
